{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/40","id":5063182038,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVOzNm88AAAABLcoG1g","html_url":"https://github.com/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pull/40","diff_url":"https://github.com/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pull/40.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pull/40.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/issues/40","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/40/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/40/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/issues/40/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/z1xel/SoftSpoken/statuses/4c7b35c2c41a65c87c94dbe74bee33ef4b4e84f2","number":40,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Show recorded book discovery locations in Writings narration headings","user":{"login":"z1xel","id":121463840,"node_id":"U_kgDOBz1kIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121463840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel","html_url":"https://github.com/z1xel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/z1xel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What changes\n\nWhen a book, letter, note, scroll or other readable has a **recorded character discovery location**, add that location to the narrator's white heading:\n\n- `Book ┬╖ Discovered in Darnassus` above `The World Tree and the Emerald Dream`.\n- `Scroll ┬╖ Discovered in Orgrimmar` for a carried readable acquired in Orgrimmar, even if read later elsewhere.\n- Multiple recorded sites are listed alphabetically, just as in the Compendium.\n- A book discovered in an older save **without** origin information retains its old narrator heading (`Book`), with no invented location.\n- When **Read Book as One Line** is off, the existing book-title heading gains the discovery label; page-number labels remain unchanged.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `SoftSpoken_Writings/DiscoveryLocations.lua`: expose the recorded-location summary already used conceptually by the Compendium as `B:KnownDiscoverySummary(bookID)` (nil when unknown), plus `B:DiscoverySummary(bookID)` for the Compendium's existing explicit unknown-origin text.\n- `SoftSpoken_Writings/UI/Readables.lua`: replace its duplicate local location-formatter with the shared function. No changes to listing, book placements or discovery events.\n- `SoftSpoken_Writings/Audio.lua`: append known origin to the **presentation heading only**. Pack choice, queue logic, file path, playback, portraits and captions are untouched.\n- Adds `tests/writings_narrator_discovery.lua` to CI. Tests live Writings code with mocks for known/unknown/legacy/acquired/multiple origins and both narration modes.\n\n## In-game verification\n\nFind/replay *The World Tree and the Emerald Dream* from the Writings Compendium (where its subtitle already says `Discovered in Darnassus`). The narrator heading should show `Book ┬╖ Discovered in Darnassus`. Replay a book with unknown recorded location: it should still say `Book`. Toggle **Read Book as One Line** off and confirm that page numbering stays intact.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-29T06:05:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T06:19:51Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T06:12:24Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T06